  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the CBD work on Digital sequence information on genetic resources (DSI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports the formal process on genetic resources (DSI) decided by the Parties to the Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD) Conference of the Parties (COP). Especially Goal C of the Global Biodiversity Framework Agreement (GBF), which underlines the urgency to increase equitable benefit-sharing arising from the utilization of genetic resources, digital sequence information on genetic resources (DSI), and traditional knowledge associated with genetic resources. From a development perspective, there are high positive socio-economic and societal impacts that benefit-sharing can create. The developing countries are highly invested in the DSI process and the fair sharing of benefits (ABS) of the resources generated. This is also true for the IPLCs and vulnerable groups and the need to protect traditional knowledge associated with genetic resources and receiving the monetary and non-monetary benefits from it. The negotiated end-result (a global fund and a multilateral mechanism for DSI) will provide funds for developing countries and IPLCs to support their implementation of the Kunming Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework.</narrative>
  </description>
